# SOLID Principles for Frontend

## S - Single Responsibility

A component/hook/function should have ONE reason to change.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD: Does too many things
function UserCard({ userId }) {
  const [user, setUser] = useState(null);
  useEffect(() => { fetchUser(userId).then(setUser) }, [userId]);
  const handleEdit = () => { /* edit logic */ };
  return <div>...</div>;
}

// ✅ GOOD: Separation of concerns
function UserCard({ user, onEdit }) {
  return <div>...</div>;  // Only renders
}

function useUser(userId) {
  return useQuery(['user', userId], () => fetchUser(userId));
}
```

## O - Open/Closed

Open for extension, closed for modification.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD: Extensible component via props
interface ButtonProps {
  variant?: 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'danger';
  size?: 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg';
  children: ReactNode;
}

function Button({ variant = 'primary', size = 'md', children }: ButtonProps) {
  return <button className={cn(variants[variant], sizes[size])}>{children}</button>;
}
```

## L - Liskov Substitution

Child components should be substitutable for their parents.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD: Specialized input extends base behavior
interface InputProps extends React.InputHTMLAttributes<HTMLInputElement> {
  label?: string;
}

function Input({ label, ...props }: InputProps) {
  return (
    <div>
      {label && <label>{label}</label>}
      <input {...props} />
    </div>
  );
}
```

## I - Interface Segregation

Small and specific interfaces.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD: Giant interface
interface UserActions {
  onCreate, onUpdate, onDelete, onView, onExport, onImport...
}

// ✅ GOOD: Segregated interfaces
interface Creatable { onCreate: () => void; }
interface Editable { onUpdate: () => void; }
interface Deletable { onDelete: () => void; }
```

## D - Dependency Inversion

Depend on abstractions, not concrete implementations.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD: Hook receives service as dependency
function useNotifications(notificationService: NotificationService) {
  return useMutation({
    mutationFn: notificationService.send,
  });
}

// Usage with different implementations
useNotifications(emailService);
useNotifications(pushService);
```

## SOLID Checklist

- [ ] Does each component have a single responsibility?
- [ ] Can I extend without modifying existing code?
- [ ] Do specialized components maintain the parent contract?
- [ ] Are interfaces small and specific?
- [ ] Are dependencies injected rather than instantiated?
